  kind of show you like this so it kind of  makes a little bit more sense to you  like you probably learned the formula  distance equals rate times time it's  very similar to that it's the rate times  the time so that's why I split it up  like this but of course T is like T over  1 so you can combine those into one  fraction okay now what we're going to do  is we're going to clear  denominators and what you want to do is  you want to multiply everything by the  common denominator so what's the  smallest thing that three two and one  all go into well that's six right so  what we're going to do is going to  multiply the entire equation by six so  we're going to distribute the 6 to the  each of the terms okay in the equation  we're doing it to both sides left and  right so it's keeping the equation  balanced so when you distribute it to  hear you're getting 60 ok divided by  three plus 60 divided by two equals six  over one but you can see the six divided  by three that's reducing or cancelling  down to two t-this is reducing you're  cancelling down to 3t and this is just  six so that's why they call it clearing  the denominators you're eliminating the  denominators so now if we combine like  terms we get five T equals six we divide  by five and you can see the time is  going to be one in one fifth of an hour  okay now if you want to convert that  into minutes 1/5 of an hour is 12  minutes right because 12 times 5 is 60  so well there you go so that's how you  do a combined rate problem just think of  it as splitting the rate in the time you  know separately and then go ahead and  add the two together to get the total  and you could have three people four  people and so on so I hope you're  enjoying the video subscribe to the  channel check out some of my past videos  and I look forward to seeing a future  video I'll talk to you soon
 

